{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1540879162,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNDE4MTU2Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2961#issuecomment-434181562"},"message":"In -revolution I do not use these helpers -- for the reason above, but also because they only query one property at a time, while pretty much all relevant properties together can be determined from a single `Repo.(annex)status()` call. Going through the top-level `rev-status` command should take care of all symlink issues (that come from this possibility of dataset and repo being in two different aparent paths -- at least those that I am aware of.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540884638,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNDE5ODQ4MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2961#issuecomment-434198481"},"message":"\u003e Quick solution of ok_file_under_git adjustment would be ok, but I am not sure if that would be the \"correct\" one...\n\nIf `ok_clean_git` isn't aware of `*Repo.path` being realpath, then yes - that's a correct solution, IMO.\nHowever, another \"solution\" is to just stop calling `ok_clean_git` with a path and pass the `*Repo` instead. We do that all the time and it's actually unnecessary (and costs to figure out what it is).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540885031,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzNDIwMDAxMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2961#issuecomment-434200010"},"message":"\u003e (although we do have .realpath for that purpose)\n\nWe do have `.realpath` and we should remove it, I think. But: It's not \"for that purpose\". It's important part of the idea, that `.path` is used that way by flyweight not that there's `realpath` somewhere.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id